---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('tare')!;
const lastUpdated = 'June 24, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Privacy Policy — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description={`How ${app.name} collects, uses, and protects your information.`}
  path={`/${app.slug}/privacy`}
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/tare">← {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p
      style="padding: 12px 14px; border: 1px solid #f0d28a; background: #fdf6e3; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 600;"
    >
      DRAFT — This policy is a working draft pending legal review. It describes
      how {app.name} is intended to handle your information and may change before
      publication.
    </p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how {COMPANY.name} (“we”, “us”) handles
      information in connection with the {app.name} application and website
      (the “Service”). {app.name} is a GLP-1 and metabolic-health tracker, so
      much of the information you enter is health-related. We aim to collect as
      little as possible and to keep what we do collect private and secure.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information.</strong> When you sign in, we use Microsoft
        identity services. We receive a unique account identifier and basic
        profile details such as your name and email address so we can create and
        secure your account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Health data you create.</strong> Content and activity you enter
        in the app — such as blood-glucose readings, medication and injection
        logs, weight and body measurements, well-being and mood notes, vitals,
        lab results, diagnoses, and medical-record entries — so the Service can
        track your journey and show your trends.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>AI summaries.</strong> If you ask for an insight, we send the
        relevant readings you logged to an AI provider to generate a summary
        grounded in your own data. Your data is not used to train AI models.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Limited technical data.</strong> Basic operational logs (such as
        request timestamps and error information) needed to run, secure, and
        troubleshoot the Service.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> collect precise location, contacts, or device
      advertising identifiers, and we do not use third-party advertising or
      cross-app tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide, maintain, and secure your account and the Service.</li>
      <li>To save your logs and show your weight, glucose, and journey trends.</li>
      <li>
        To generate AI summaries grounded in the data you choose to share, only
        when you request them.
      </li>
      <li>To diagnose problems and improve reliability and performance.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How your information is stored and protected</h2>
    <p>
      Your health data is stored in your own per-user private SQLite database —
      your own file, not a shared multi-tenant database. Information is encrypted
      in transit using HTTPS, and the Service is hosted on Microsoft Azure.
      Access is limited to what is necessary to operate the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. We share information only with
      infrastructure providers that host and secure the Service (for example,
      Microsoft Azure for hosting and identity, and an AI provider for the
      summaries you request), and only as needed to operate it, or where
      required by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your information for as long as your account is active. You can
      export your data as JSON at any time, and you may request access to, or
      deletion of, your account and associated data by emailing
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is intended for a general, adult audience and is not directed
      to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
      children.
    </p>

    <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} helps you record and review your own health information,
      including optional AI-generated summaries. It does not provide medical
      advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always consult a qualified healthcare
      professional about your care.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be
      reflected by updating the “Last updated” date above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
